<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PlateVault MSI strings for en-US, wired in through
  bundle > windows > wix > language in tauri.conf.json.

  The MSI shows bundle > licenseFile (installer/privacy-notice.txt, set in
  tauri.windows.conf.json) on WixUI's license dialog. These strings override
  WixUI's own, so that dialog reads as a privacy notice the user has read,
  not a licence agreement (SignPath condition b, astro-plan-vmxcu).
  installer/nsis-hooks.nsh does the same for the NSIS setup.exe. Keep
  privacy-notice.txt in step with docs/manual/11-privacy.md.

  WixUI's license dialog needs RTF. Tauri writes it from the same .txt at
  build time (tauri-bundler 2.10.2, msi/mod.rs:576-596): it wraps the text
  in an RTF header with code page 1252 and turns each line break into \par,
  with no escaping. NSIS shows the .txt itself. So privacy-notice.txt stays
  plain ASCII with no backslash or curly braces, and it must not be renamed
  to .rtf, which Tauri would pass to WiX unconverted.

  At build time Tauri appends its own default strings (LaunchApp,
  DowngradeErrorMessage and the rest) to this file. It skips any default
  whose Id attribute, written as Id="...", appears anywhere in this file,
  comments included. So this file lists only the strings PlateVault changes,
  and its comments never quote a Tauri string id in that form.
-->
<WixLocalization Culture="en-us" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/localization">
  <String Id="LicenseAgreementDlgTitle">{\WixUI_Font_Title}Privacy notice</String>
  <String Id="LicenseAgreementDlgDescription">What PlateVault sends over the internet, and how to turn it off</String>
  <String Id="LicenseAgreementDlgLicenseAcceptedCheckBox">I have &amp;read the privacy notice</String>
</WixLocalization>
